WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.100
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.033
I'm hanging out with
Drew Barrymore, everybody.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.467
Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.868
Every morning. I watch you.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.567
We're about to play a brand-new
game called "Focus Up."

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.734
Here we go.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:17.734
-♪ F-o-o-o-o-ocus Up ♪

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.200
-Alright.
Here's how this works.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.834
We're gonna be shown a series
of pixilated images

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:24.033
that are slowly
going to come into focus.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.467
Okay? Now, once you think that
you know what the image is,

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.601
you hit this buzzer right here.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.067
If you guess right,
you win a point.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.067
We're gonna play three rounds
with different categories.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.334
-I'm excited.
-You ready to play?

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.868
-Yes, 'cause we're both
very competitive.

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.701
-Our first category is...

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.267
[ Beeping ]

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.367
-Album covers?

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.167
Oh, did I ruin it?
-Whoa.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.901
-Sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.067
Sorry.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.300
-Did you know
it was album covers?

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.434
-No, I think it's, like,
a professional faux pas.

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.100
I saw a monitor,
and I was like --

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.934
my inner voice was like,
"Read it!"

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:53.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.634
-That's correct.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:59.234
You did do --
But this is not planned.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:00.868
Did you know
that it's album covers?

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:03.968
-It says it in the monitor.
-I know, but...

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.200
People watching at home
might think this is rigged.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.968
-[Stiffly] You're right, Jimmy.
I didn't know.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.801
-You -- Hold on a second.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:17.834
Do you know the answers
to this game?

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.801
-I am not purposefully
looking in the monitor now.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.367
I can tell you that.
-No, no, you have to.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.000
No, but -- I mean,
I don't know what this is.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.601
-Are you looking
in the monitor?

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.234
Does it have the answer
in there?

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.200
-No. It's the category.
-Okay.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.701
It also says, "Okay, Drew,
let's focus up."

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.334
[ Applause ]

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.734
-Alright.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.734
It's not even hooked up
to anything.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:47.234
Alright. Let's see --
-I hope it is.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.200
-Alright. Here we go.
Let's see the first blur.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.868
Drew, let's focus up.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.267
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.501
And start moving it.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:55.133
Whenever you're ready,
press the buzzer.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.334
It's green. Is it Kermit?

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:58.968
No.
-That would be amazing.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.334
-What is it again?
Album covers. Oh.

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.367
-"Let It Be"! "Abbey --"
-"Abbey Road."

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.434
Blblblblblblbl!
You're right, you're right.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:09.767
Good job.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:13.033
See?
That's the thing about Jimmy.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.801
It's all fun and games
until it's game time.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:18.267
[ Laughter ]
-Then it's not fun?

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.133
I'm really competitive.
Alright. Here we go. Alright.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.534
-He will not let you win.
-Alright. Yes, I will!

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:25.133
Let's focus up. Here we go.
It's an album cover.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.567
Go.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.400
-Again? Album cover?
-Is it Flee--

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.634
Fleetwood Mac. "Rumors."

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:31.834
[ Bell dings ]

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.501
Whoa! [ Laughs ]

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:42.000
[ Humming "Sanford and Son"
theme song ]

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.734
♪♪

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.868
Wow! That one. Come on, now.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.634
-That was --
-That was pretty impressive.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.234
-That was insane.
-Yeah. Good.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.100
This game is the best game
in the world!

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.968
Alright. Here we go.
Time for round two.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.734
Alright.
Let's get our next category.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:01.234
Here we go.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.467
[ Beeping ]

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.834
Alright, buddy.
-Okay.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:05.868
-Sitcoms.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.267
-Okay.
-Sitcoms.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.400
Alright. Let's focus up.
-Okay.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.601
-I'm focused.
Alright. Sitcoms?

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.567
Okay. Go.

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:17.834
♪♪

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:20.901
Ohh. "ER."

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.434
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.067
Oh, I know what it is!

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.067
-Wait. Do we get to keep going?
-Yeah, you can keep going.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.067
But then you buzz in.
You get the first buzz.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.634
-I do?
-Go.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.901
-You're just giving it to me.
-You know what it is.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.234
Just say it.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.033
-"Designing Women"?

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.434
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.601
-Wait. I was going to say
"Designing Women,"

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.701
but now I'm changing it.
It's "Facts of Life."

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:43.267
-[ Bell dinging ]
-Ohh!

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.434
-I thought it was
"Golden Girls."

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.033
-There was too many
for "Golden Girls."

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.567
-Yeah, there were
too many, but, yeah.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.067
-Oh, gosh darn it.
-Tootie. Come on.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:51.300
Alright. Here we go.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.968
-Tootie, Blair, Jo,
Natalie, and Mrs. Garrett.

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:56.334
-Mrs. Garrett! Come on!
Alright.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:59.100
Alright. Let's focus up.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.434
♪♪

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:04.033
-This -- This is hard.
-No, it's very hard.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:07.701
♪♪

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:11.033
Ah! It's got to be
"Golden Girls."

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.868
-"Family Ties."

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:14.634
[ Bell dings ]
-It's "Family Ties."

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.267
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:21.067
[ Speaking indistinctly ]
-No, I didn't.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:22.868
Oh, we have one more!
-Yeah, we have one more.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.534
-One more, one more!
-We have one more.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:27.601
-I don't think I can win.
-Gosh. "Family Ties."

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.300
-I can't win.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.968
-Of course, they're a family.
They're tied together! I get it!

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.567
-I know. That's actually
a disturbing image.

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.167
-I've never seen that
in my life.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.634
I've never seen that.
-Never.

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:39.267
It's like way too much tied up.
-One of the best shows ever.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.767
-That's like family in crisis.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.567
Yeah. "Family Held Hostage."

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.033
-Seriously?
That's a real picture?

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.467
-I don't know, man. Yeah.
-What were they thinking?

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:51.167
-I like it. I get it.
Now I'm into it.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.234
-No, no. It goes way too far.
It's dark.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.767
-We have a third one
for this category.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.133
Here we go.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:58.133
Alright. Go.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.734
-Okay. Is it still sitcoms?

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.734
-Yeah, sitcoms.
-Okay.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:06.234
Oh, it's two people.
-"Cagney and Lacey"!

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.434
Oh, wait.
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.400
-"Bosom Buddies"?
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.601
No. "Perfect Strangers."

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.267
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:14.234
-Alright.
Let it go a little more.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.400
Those were really good guesses.
-Hall and Oates?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.200
♪♪

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.734
Ohh! "Laverne and Shirley"!
Come on!

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:22.868
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.133
These are pictures
we've never seen.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:26.434
They're odd photos
of classic sitcoms.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.467
-Yeah.
-That's a different game.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:30.267
"Odd Photos of Classic Sitcoms."

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:34.400
You ever see
Kojak skateboarding?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.234
No.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:37.701
How would I guess "Kojak"?

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:39.400
Alright.
-Oh, final round.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.033
-This is the --
-Wait. Oh, God.

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:43.100
How come none of our numbers
are moving?

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.567
I guess we just didn't get any
the last few rounds.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:48.067
-No. It's 3-1.
You still have time to win.

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:49.934
This last one
is worth 10,000 points.

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:51.567
-Oh, perfect! Okay, great!

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.934
-It's the mystery round, Drew.
The mystery round.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:55.667
-Oh. We need more mystery?
-We don't know the category.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.601
-It's mystery on mystery.
Oh, we don't know the category.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.300
-No, we don't know the category.
It's a mystery.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.501
-Okay.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:01.968
-Whoever gets this
wins everything.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:03.000
-Really?
-Yes.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.334
-You're just changing it
to make it fun

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:06.434
because I'm losing.
-No. No, it's not true.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:07.968
-Alright. Well, let's see --
-Let's see the final image.

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:09.601
Here we go.
-I -- Hm.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.334
-Okay.

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:18.434
Any -- Before we start playing,
any guesses?

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:19.601
-Oh.

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:21.400
-Looks like the paint aisle
in Home Depot.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.834
-Yeah.
[ Buzzer ]

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:25.868
-Oh, no, I'm kidding. Alright.
Alright, ready? Let's start.

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:30.634
♪♪

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:35.400
♪♪

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.801
Ohh! Come on.
"Fever Pitch."

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.133
-Aww.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:41.701
[ Bell dinging ]

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:45.467
My thanks to Drew Barrymore.
I'm giving it to you, bud.

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:47.234
The best.

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:49.467
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show." Stick around.

